{
  "decision": "replace_ranges",
  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a large, sustained jump in all components around index 546–547 (e.g., N from ~-4 to +7.87, E from ~12 to 27, U from ~2 to 6), followed by a return to pre-jump levels by index 555–556. P1 (532–546) ends just before the jump and does not include the return; its onset offset is small (-0.2, +0.3, +1.1), inconsistent with the observed ~12–15 mm jump. P2 (538–554) starts before the jump but ends before full return (index 554 vs return evident at 555+); its onset offset (+13, +15.8, +4.5) matches the jump magnitude but misaligns the return boundary. The visual interval analysis identifies best pair (538, 555) with high continuous criteria, supporting a single genuine temporary platform from ~538 to ~555. Neither P1 nor P2 correctly captures both onset and return; thus replace with a single range covering the full offset-return event.",
  "pair_ids": ["538-555"]
}
